raph.json, so a bad or partial re-extraction can never silently shrink a good graph; issue #479.", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_concept_empty_graph_guard", "label": "Empty-graph guard before write (#1392)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Immediately after build_from_json, if G.number_of_nodes() == 0 the pipeline aborts before any write, because an empty extraction (all files skipped, binary-only corpus, or a failed extraction) must never clobber an existing good graph.json/GRAPH_REPORT.md.", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_concept_graph_health_check", "label": "Graph health check (diagnose_extraction)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_concept_subagent_dispatch_mandate", "label": "Mandatory parallel general-purpose subagent dispatch", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Semantic extraction subagents must be dispatched as subagent_type=general-purpose (never Explore, which is read-only and cannot write chunk files to disk, silently dropping extraction results) and all in one message so they run in parallel; reading files one-by-one instead is 5-10x slower.", "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_skills_graphify_skill_doc", "target": "claude_skills_graphify_references_add_watch_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/graphify/SKILL.md", "sou